---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

import { supportContact } from '../config';

const lastUpdated = '2026-10-19';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How plank.to handles your data: local storage, device backups, notifications, optional weather and location sharing with Open-Meteo, and what is not collected."
>
  <div class="container">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      plank.to is a daily planner that keeps your plans on your device. It has no accounts, no cloud
      sync, no analytics, and no ads.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Last updated:</strong>
      <time datetime={lastUpdated}>19 October 2026</time>
    </p>
    <p role="note">
      <strong>Draft.</strong> This policy has not yet been reviewed by a lawyer for the countries
      where the app will be released. It describes how the app works today and may change after that
      review.
    </p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-labelledby="toc-heading">
      <h2 id="toc-heading">On this page</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="#summary">Summary</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#local-data">Data stored on your device</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#backups">Device backups</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#notifications">Notifications</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#weather">Weather and location</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#attribution">Attribution</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#retention">Caching and retention</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#not-collected">What we do not do</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#website">This website</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#changes">Changes and contact</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="summary">Summary</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your tasks, routines, notes, and settings are saved on your device.</li>
      <li>
        Plank does not run a server for the app, so it cannot see your plans or your location.
      </li>
      <li>
        Weather is off by default. If you turn it on, the app contacts Open-Meteo, a third party,
        with an approximate location.
      </li>
      <li>Reminders are off by default and are created on your device.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="local-data">Data stored on your device</h2>
    <p>
      The app saves what you enter in a database on your device: tasks, weekly routines,
      notes, reminder settings, clothing preferences, display settings, and, if you use weather,
      your saved place and the last forecast. This data is not sent to Plank or to anyone else by
      the app. Deleting the app removes this data from the device, subject to the backup note below.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can clear the saved weather place at any time ("Remove location" or turning weather off).
      The reset buttons in Settings only restore appearance, reminder, and clothing choices to their
      defaults; they do not delete your tasks, routines, or saved weather place.
    </p>

    <h2 id="backups">Device backups</h2>
    <p>
      Plank keeps your data in one database file in the app's storage on your phone, and it does not
      opt out of your phone's backups. If iCloud Backup, a computer backup, or Android's Google
      backup is turned on, your phone may include that file: your tasks, routines, notes, settings,
      saved weather place, and the last forecast. A copy may then be stored by Apple or Google under
      their terms, and it can be restored to a new phone. Plank does not control, see, or delete
      those backups. For this reason we do not promise that your data never leaves your device. To
      avoid it, turn off backup in your phone's settings (on iPhone you can switch it off for Plank
      alone).
    </p>

    <h2 id="notifications">Notifications</h2>
    <p>
      Reminders are optional. The app asks for notification permission only after you choose to turn
      reminders on. Reminders are local notifications scheduled on your device; they do not go
      through a Plank server or a push service run by Plank. If you decline permission, the planner
      still works. You can change the permission at any time in your device settings.
    </p>

    <h2 id="weather">Weather and location</h2>
    <p>
      Weather is optional and off by default. Until you turn it on, the app makes no weather or
      place-search requests. If you turn it on, you choose how to give a place:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Device location.</strong> The app asks for location permission only at that point,
        while the app is in use, and never in the background. It takes a single approximate fix when
        a forecast is needed and rounds it to two decimal places (about 1 km) before saving or
        sending it. The precise position is discarded.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Search for a place.</strong> You type a city or postcode. The search text is sent to
        Open-Meteo's place-search service. The text is not saved; only the place you pick is saved,
        with rounded coordinates.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h3>What is sent to Open-Meteo</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        For a forecast: the rounded latitude and longitude, which weather details to return (such as
        temperature, precipitation, and wind), a request for the local time zone, and unit choices.
      </li>
      <li>For a place search: your search text and the app's display language.</li>
      <li>
        Like any internet request, Open-Meteo also sees your device's network (IP) address and the
        time of the request.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h3>What is never sent</h3>
    <p>
      Your tasks, routines, notes, reminder content, clothing preferences, settings, precise
      location, or any account, device, or advertising identifier. The app sets no cookies for these
      requests and contains no analytics or crash-reporting tools that would pass your location on.
    </p>
    <p>
      Open-Meteo handles these requests under its own terms and privacy policy, which apply to its
      handling of them. See <a href="https://open-meteo.com/en/terms">open-meteo.com/en/terms</a>.
      Plank does not receive a copy of your requests.
    </p>

    <h2 id="attribution">Attribution</h2>
    <p>
      Weather data is provided by <a href="https://open-meteo.com/">Open-Meteo.com</a> and used
      under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 license (CC BY 4.0).
    </p>

    <h2 id="retention">Caching and retention</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The app keeps only the most recent forecast for your one saved place, on your device. It
        refreshes at most about every 30 minutes while the app is open and the forecast is visible,
        and never in the background.
      </li>
      <li>
        A forecast older than about 3 hours is shown as out of date, with its age. A cached forecast
        is discarded after 24 hours.
      </li>
      <li>
        Your saved place and forecast stay until you remove the location, turn weather off, change
        how you set your place, or delete the app. No search history or previous locations are kept.
      </li>
      <li>Your planner data stays on the device until you delete it or delete the app.</li>
      <li>
        Plank keeps no copy on a server, so there is nothing on our side to retain or delete.
        Open-Meteo's own retention is described in its policy, and device backups are covered above.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="not-collected">What we do not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No account, sign-in, or profile.</li>
      <li>No cloud sync of your planner data.</li>
      <li>No analytics, tracking, or advertising, and no advertising identifiers.</li>
      <li>No selling or sharing of your data. Plank has none to sell or share.</li>
      <li>No background location tracking.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The app is free and stays non-commercial. This is also a condition of using Open-Meteo's free
      service; if that ever changes, this policy will be updated first.
    </p>

    <h2 id="website">This website</h2>
    <p>
      This website is a static site with product information. It does not collect or display your
      planner data and does not connect to your planner. It sets no cookies and has no analytics.
      Like any website, the host that serves it may keep standard technical server logs.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the date above will change and significant changes will be described
      here.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Contact{supportContact.isPlaceholder ? ' (placeholder)' : ''}:</strong>{' '}
      {supportContact.value}.
      {supportContact.isPlaceholder &&
        ' A maintained support route has not been chosen yet, so this is not a working address.'}
      See the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
